    "title": "Glowing tribute to a dependable friend",
    "body": [
      "Jide (Akogó 1), as we, your close friends used to call you, when the news of your home call was broken to me, I thought I was dreaming because we still discussed on the Tuesday morning as the surgery was earlier fixed for Wednesday and we never thought that the surgery would be carried out later on that Tuesday. I was about to call you that evening when I received the call announcing your death to me. Over that night, I wasn't myself again as I developed high fever which took me about ten days before I fully recovered.",
      "Jide, I will not be doing your family and myself justice if I fail to write this tribute in view of our closeness dating back to almost six decades of friendship (1967-2026).",
      "Among the friends I had ever moved closely with, you stood out as a true friend whom I can never forget in life as long as I still have breath in me.",
      "Much as I would have loved to be very brief in my write-up, I can't do without making every reader of this Tribute to know the type of \"true friend\" you were made of in going to any length to save any friend you have studied and known his/her character in terms of honesty and accountability in the discharge of his/her official duties.",
      "On this fateful day in December, 1979, I came to meet you in your office and told you that I had a problem with the then Kwara State Head of Service (HOS) in connection with the items I purchased for my office before proceeding to Kaduna Polytechnic on course, on the strength of the serious false allegation the officer who relieved me made against me that I didn't buy anything with the money given to me - whereas I bought all the items at the Kwara State Government owned Midland Stores at Ilorin with Local Purchase Order (LPO) that did not involve cash. These items were duly taken on charge in Store Ledger and Store Receipt Voucher, which this officer duly signed for and took over from me before I proceeded on course. Luckily enough, I put up with you when I came to Ilorin to purchase them and you knew everything about the items.",
      "To this end, the then HOS who was the Permanent Secretary of Commerce that approved the Authority to Incur Expenditure (AIE) forgot that it wasn't CASH he approved for me, said that I should be recalled back from Kaduna to come and face a panel of inquiry to clear myself first. The Kaduna Polytechnic did not even inform me concerning the recall letter which they ignored hence I didn't hear anything from home concerning the recall until I came home on Christmas holiday.",
      "Two teams of Auditors were engaged to carry out the auditing -- Divisional Auditor's Office at Lokoja and the other from State Auditor General's Office at Ilorin. They both came out with the same verdict of *\"NO FRAUD WAS FOUND.\"* When I came to Ilorin to receive my Course Allowance, the HOS was still bent on recalling me back from the course. When I heard this, I had to come to you, Jide, to inform you about the development and you left your work immediately and asked me to follow you to the office of the HOS. On entering into his office, you went on your knees and I had to go on my knees as well. In the course of your telling him of our mission to his office, one of the former Permanent Secretaries of the Ministry of Commerce and Industry came in and met us on our knees, then cut in and asked the HOS, \"Is it about me we were both kneeling?\" And the HOS said yes. He then said, \"I think you know me that I will be the last person to ever condone indiscipline in the Civil Service, but I can categorically tell you that Johnson was one of the most hardworking and honest officers I worked with in the Ministry, and as such, I am pleading on his behalf that you please forgive him. The HOS had no alternative than to burst into laughter and said that \"I was lucky to have two of the most respected Top Civil Servants pleading on my behalf, and as such, he has pardoned me. All this while, you remained on your knees. I CAN NEVER FORGET THE TYPE OF LOVE YOU DEMONSTRATED FOR ME AS A TRUE FRIEND WHO COULD GO TO ANY LENGTH TO SAVE A TRUSTED FRIEND WHEN IN TROUBLE. I then went back to complete my studies successfully. GOD WILL REWARD YOUR CHILDREN BOUNTIFULLY WHEREVER THEY GO IN LIFE. THERE SHALL BE READY HELPERS FOR THEM AT ANY POINT OF THEIR NEEDS, IN THE GRACIOUS NAME OF JESUS AMEN.",
      "Jide, as a result of your honesty and accountability, you almost lost your life at Kaduna when you went on official assignment to recover debts for your then employer - Bank of Industry, when you suffered a deadly spiritual attack, because you refused to compromise your Oath of Office when some debtors tried to lure you into agreeing to be bribed in order to write off their debts. They pleaded that you should take some millions of naira thereby classifying their debts as \"bad debts.\" Instead, you asked them to pay the moneys into the BOI's coffers as \"part payments\" of their debts.",
      "You stood for \"the truth\" on any matter irrespective of whose ox was gored, because your \"Motto in life was *\"FIDELITY UNTO DEATH. \"* You knew the Truth and stuck to it tenaciously (John 8:32), definitely, the Lord Jesus Christ has received you into His bosom, where you will be rewarded with eternal rest. My prayer is that, may your Children take after you in upholding the Truth, as you did, under any circumstance, and God Almighty shall continue to be their strength and Refuge all the days of their lives, in the peerless name of Jesus Christ. May He grant the entire family and friends the fortitude to bear the great loss Amen.",
      "Rest in Perfect Peace, Jide and tell Helen that we greatly miss you both. Adieu, the brave and truthful Couple!!!"
    ]
