      "Less than a week before your demise, I visited you on your hospital bed in Ela Hospital, near Niger Basin, Ilorin. The hospital is owned and run by a schoolmate and senior of mine in the sixties at the Provincial Secondary School turned Government Secondary School Dekina. On that sunny afternoon, you were joyful, lively and full of your usual rib-cracking, wisecracks. It was difficult, aside from being in bed, to believe you were truly in pain and awaiting a surgical procedure. After our usual jangle and banters, we parted on a note that I would come to see you on my return. And you bid me safe journey. \" Olu, take care. See you when you return' with another humorous remark. There was no death in your eyes, as we say in our part of the world, in literal translation.",
